  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The force on the rod due to the magnetic field and gravity is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />Hence the extension in the springs is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> that effective spring constant is 2k)<br /><br />Therefore the length of the spring is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0065305_Ans.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 215px; height: 152px;\" />",
